{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y4MLoqemYKasysQKsrCgWj","type":"tool_result","content":".gitignore\nREADME.md\nlogs/bug-report.md\nlogs/prod-error.log\nsrc/app.py\ntests/fake_dynamo.py\ntests/test_feed.py\n# Hidden story still in the public feed (staging)\n\nDate: 2026-08-05\nReporter: Dasha (content)\nEnvironment: staging, table `stories-staging`, build 2026-08-04 (same as prod)\n\nThe Hide button on staging gives a 500 (same error as prod, see\nprod-error.log), so I hid \"my-first-week\" by hand with the AWS CLI:\n\n    aws dynamodb update-item --table-name stories-staging \\\n      --key '{\"slug\":{\"S\":\"my-first-week\"}}' \\\n      --update-expression 'SET #h = :t' \\\n      --expression-attribute-names '{\"#h\":\"hidden\"}' \\\n      --expression-attribute-values '{\":t\":{\"BOOL\":true}}'\n\n`get-item` afterwards shows `hidden: true` on the item, so the write landed.\nBut `GET /feed` on staging still lists \"my-first-week\" -- ten minutes later,\nafter a redeploy, and in a private browser window. Nothing in the logs,\nno error, the feed call returns 200.\n\nIs the feed cached somewhere? Or does the feed read from a different table?\n2026-08-04T09:12:41Z INFO  api.hide_story slug=why-i-left-mobx user=vk\n2026-08-04T09:12:41Z ERROR api.hide_story unhandled exception\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/var/task/api.py\", line 61, in hide_story\n    library.hide(slug, by=user)\n  File \"/var/task/src/app.py\", line 53, in hide\n    self.table.update_item(\n  File \"/var/task/boto3/resources/factory.py\", line 581, in do_action\n    response = action(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/var/task/boto3/resources/action.py\", line 88, in __call__\n    response = getattr(parent.meta.client, operation_name)(*args, **params)\n  File \"/var/task/botocore/client.py\", line 569, in _api_call\n    return self._make_api_call(operation_name, kwargs)\n  File \"/var/task/botocore/client.py\", line 1023, in _make_api_call\n    raise error_class(parsed_response, operation_name)\nbotocore.exceptions.ClientError: An error occurred (ValidationException) when calling the UpdateItem operation: Invalid UpdateExpression: Attribute name is a reserved keyword; reserved keyword: hidden\n2026-08-04T09:12:41Z INFO  api.hide_story -> 500\n2026-08-04T09:14:02Z INFO  api.hide_story slug=why-i-left-mobx user=vk\n2026-08-04T09:14:02Z ERROR api.hide_story unhandled exception\nbotocore.exceptions.ClientError: An error occurred (ValidationException) when calling the UpdateItem operation: Invalid UpdateExpression: Attribute name is a reserved keyword; reserved keyword: hidden\n2026-08-04T09:14:02Z INFO  api.hide_story -> 500","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a08a04c-3f1c-4797-98e7-f2dcbab8a0ac","uuid":"ed5ce28f-deea-410a-a4aa-96d54c6707be","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:38:19.334Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".gitignore\nREADME.md\nlogs/bug-report.md\nlogs/prod-error.log\nsrc/app.py\ntests/fake_dynamo.py\ntests/test_feed.py\n# Hidden story still in the public feed (staging)\n\nDate: 2026-08-05\nReporter: Dasha (content)\nEnvironment: staging, table `stories-staging`, build 2026-08-04 (same as prod)\n\nThe Hide button on staging gives a 500 (same error as prod, see\nprod-error.log), so I hid \"my-first-week\" by hand with the AWS CLI:\n\n    aws dynamodb update-item --table-name stories-staging \\\n      --key '{\"slug\":{\"S\":\"my-first-week\"}}' \\\n      --update-expression 'SET #h = :t' \\\n      --expression-attribute-names '{\"#h\":\"hidden\"}' \\\n      --expression-attribute-values '{\":t\":{\"BOOL\":true}}'\n\n`get-item` afterwards shows `hidden: true` on the item, so the write landed.\nBut `GET /feed` on staging still lists \"my-first-week\" -- ten minutes later,\nafter a redeploy, and in a private browser window. Nothing in the logs,\nno error, the feed call returns 200.\n\nIs the feed cached somewhere? Or does the feed read from a different table?\n2026-08-04T09:12:41Z IN